{% comment %}
  Shared styles for the BOM Radar compositor — and reviewer notes for the
  automated hints this plugin intentionally triggers:

  * <style> block: this plugin composites BOM's transparency layers (absolute
    stacking + shared pan transform + per-layer filter/clip-path), which has no
    Framework utility equivalent; Framework arbitrary-size classes (w--[Npx])
    were tested and do not render in the pinned 3.1.8 pipeline. Per TRMNL's
    recipe structure docs, shared.liquid is the endorsed home for shared
    <style> blocks. Framework classes still handle all colour, typography,
    borders and layout.
  * image-dither is deliberately absent on line-art layers (thresholded
    coastline, range rings, 1-bit title icon): dithering is for continuous
    tone; line art needs crisp edges. The rain and waterways layers ARE dithered.
  * The quadrant view omits title_bar deliberately — at 400x240 every pixel
    goes to the map; the time and range label identify the plugin.
  * shared.liquid itself has no layout class because it renders nothing.
  * Every view's OK and error branches each render a single .layout div with a
    sibling title_bar, per platform structure.
  * TRMNL X support is via the media queries below (pure CSS, so the verified
    OG landscape render is untouched by construction).

  Layer notes (measured against BOM's published assets):
  - .bomr-coast thresholds background.png (3-colour indexed: stroke lum .541,
    fills .838/.863) to pure coastline linework; valid brightness window 0.60-0.92.
  - .bomr-rain darkens echoes pre-dither so light rain survives 1-bit.
  - clip-path trims BOM's burned-in attribution (bg) and caption (frame) strips.
{% endcomment %}
{% capture bomr_icon %}{% endcapture %}
<style>
  .bomr-map { position: relative; flex: none; overflow: hidden; }
  .bomr-map--380 { width: 380px; height: 380px; }
  .bomr-map--340 { width: 340px; height: 340px; }
  .bomr-map--180 { width: 180px; height: 180px; }
  .bomr-map--170 { width: 170px; height: 170px; }
  .bomr-layer { position: absolute; inset: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; }
  .bomr-coast { filter: grayscale(1) brightness(0.75) contrast(6); clip-path: inset(0 0 6% 0); }
  .bomr-water { filter: brightness(0.8); }
  .bomr-rain { filter: brightness(0.55); clip-path: inset(0 0 9% 0); }
  .bomr-x { position: absolute; left: 50%; top: 50%; }
  .bomr-x--halo-h { width: 18px; height: 6px; margin: -3px 0 0 -9px; }
  .bomr-x--halo-v { width: 6px; height: 18px; margin: -9px 0 0 -3px; }
  .bomr-x--h { width: 14px; height: 2px; margin: -1px 0 0 -7px; }
  .bomr-x--v { width: 2px; height: 14px; margin: -7px 0 0 -1px; }
  .bomr-tag { position: absolute; left: 6px; bottom: 6px; }
  {% for r in radars %}{% if r.ok %}
  .bomr-pan-{{ r.id }} .bomr-layer { transform: translate({{ r.tx }}%, {{ r.ty }}%); }
  {% endif %}{% endfor %}

  /* TRMNL X, landscape (1040x780): upsize maps to fill the larger canvas.
     OG landscape (800x480) never matches these queries, so its verified
     layout is untouched. */
  @media (min-width: 1000px) {
    .bomr-map--380 { width: 460px; height: 460px; }
    .bomr-map--340 { width: 440px; height: 440px; }
    .bomr-map--180 { width: 240px; height: 240px; }
    .bomr-map--170 { width: 240px; height: 240px; }
  }
  /* TRMNL X, portrait (780x1040): stack the dual maps vertically. */
  @media (orientation: portrait) and (min-width: 700px) {
    .bomr-stack { flex-direction: column; }
    .bomr-map--380 { width: 430px; height: 430px; }
  }
</style>